Telluric eigenspectra
---------------------
HDUs: MEAN [4447] = T0; EIGVEC [7, 4447] in the order O2 1-3, H2O 1-4, zero outside the bands; PIXMASK [4447]; COEFF = KEY (the observation) and C1-C7.
Grid: observed-frame vacuum log10 lambda = 3.5502 + 1e-4 i. Vectors are residuals R = f / model - 1.
Use through programs_telluric/tellapply.py: f_corr = f / C, ivar_corr = ivar C^2.

  survey  C                       no correction red of   observations  objects (galaxy, quasar, featureless WD)
  dr8     1 + T0 + sum a_k T_k    9200 A                  639          14,396 (10,605, 6,062, 96)
  dr17    1 + T0                  9280 A                 1377          17,078 (8,879, 12,565, 127)
  desi    1 + T0                  9280 A                 2539          23,936 (12,287, 20,000, 628)

dr8 = SDSS-I/II (MJD < 55025), dr17 = BOSS / eBOSS (MJD >= 55025). The object counts are those entering the observation means; the populations
in brackets are all objects loaded before that cut, so they sum to more than the total.
On dr17 and desi the a_k are fitted and recorded but do not enter C. dr17 H2O 1 is sky-line spikes and is never used.

  var / null of each component (var >= 1.5 x null selects it), and correlation with the guide optical depth:
           O2 1          O2 2          O2 3          H2O 1         H2O 2         H2O 3         H2O 4
  dr8      22.32 +0.83   2.61 -0.12    2.22 +0.02    4.80 +0.15    5.46 -0.04    5.15 +0.60    3.29 +0.19
  dr17      1.88 +0.95   2.34 -0.28    1.92 -0.01    2.18  0.00    2.37 +0.50    2.38 +0.35    2.06 +0.02
  desi      1.58 +0.96   1.04 +0.20    1.16 -0.20    1.30 +0.45    1.90 +0.37    1.95 +0.11    1.68 +0.08

Known limits: the 9280-9880 A water band is uncorrected (sky-dominated). DESI components are not confirmed between populations
(galaxy x quasar coefficients r <= 0.135 on the same tiles). T0 cannot separate the atmosphere from any other fixed observed-frame
residual. On DR8 a small stellar contribution to C is not excluded (a_k against TiO and Ca triplet strength, |r| up to 0.24).


